    <ferc:AttestationTitle id="f-84" contextRef="c-52">Vice President</ferc:AttestationTitle>
    <ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock id="f-85" contextRef="c-52">&lt;div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos; font-weight: bold; background-color: unset; font-size: 1em; text-align: inherit"&gt;The Company&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class="Section_1"&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; line-height: 116%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos"&gt;Tri-States NGL Pipeline, L.L.C. (the &amp;quot;Company&amp;quot;), a Delaware limited liability company, is owned 83.33 percent by Enterprise Products Operating LLC, (&amp;quot;Enterprise&amp;quot;) and 16.67 percent by Third Coast Emerald, LLC. Enterprise serves as operator of the Company.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;br /&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; line-height: 116%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos; font-weight: bold"&gt;Description of the Property&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; line-height: 116%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos"&gt;The Company owns a 167-mile natural gas liquids (NGLs) pipeline that transports mixed NGLs from Mobile Bay, Alabama to points near Kenner, Louisiana.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos"&gt;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; line-height: 116%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; line-height: 116%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos; font-weight: bold"&gt;Basis of Accounting&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; line-height: 116%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos"&gt;The accounting policies followed in preparation of these financial statements conform to those required by FERC. Financial statements are prepared on the accrual basis of accounting. Property, plant, and equipment assets are recorded at original cost.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; line-height: 116%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; line-height: 116%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos; font-weight: bold"&gt;Revenue Recognition&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; line-height: 116%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos"&gt;Revenues are derived from transportation of NGLs under an interstate tariff. The tariff specifies the amounts to be paid by shippers for service between receipt and delivery locations and the general terms and conditions of transportation services on the pipeline system. Revenue is recognized upon delivery of product to shippers.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; line-height: 116%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos"&gt;During 2025, the Company rebilled shippers for under-recovery resulting from the vacated January 20, 2022 rehearing order (Docket No. RM20-14-001) in the amount of $1,889,595.98. (See Commission's order issued on November 20, 2025 (Docket No. RM93-11-003, paragraph 37, footnote 111)). These revenues are reported in account 645 &amp;quot;Unusual or Infrequent Items (credit)&amp;quot; on page 114.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; line-height: 116%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; line-height: 116%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos; font-weight: bold"&gt;Income Taxes&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; line-height: 116%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos"&gt;The Company is a limited liability company that passes income tax liability through the company to its members and does not recognize this liability on the company's financial statements. For purposes of calculating income taxes for the annual cost of service (shown on page 700 of the Annual Report), the Company employs FERC's Policy Statement on Income Tax Allowances.&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; line-height: 116%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos"&gt;&amp;#160;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; line-height: 116%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos; font-weight: bold"&gt;Employees&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 			&lt;p style="margin-top: 0; margin-bottom: 8pt; line-height: 116%"&gt; 				&lt;span style="font-family: Aptos"&gt;The Company does not have any employees. The Company reimburses Enterprise for the allocated cost of employees who perform operating, management and other administrative functions for the Company pursuant to an operating agreement between the Company and Enterprise.&lt;br /&gt;&lt;/span&gt; 			&lt;/p&gt; 		&lt;/div&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:NotesToFinancialStatementsTextBlock>
